WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:12.371
Aisha Coleman: Good morning, Tyler. Good morning, Linda. Aisha Coleman here from Invoca. How are things in Tacoma today?

2
00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:21.727
Tyler Reed: Morning, Aisha. It's been a busy week. We're getting into the fall lending push, so lots of calls coming in.

3
00:00:22.206 --> 00:00:29.747
Linda Sorensen: Hi Aisha. Yes, we're in good shape. Just trying to keep the member experience team ahead of the volume.

4
00:00:30.122 --> 00:00:40.140
Aisha Coleman: That's great to hear. I wanted to do a quick check-in on onboarding logistics and make sure we're aligned on the next few weeks.

5
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.645
Aisha Coleman: Is now still an okay time?

6
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:48.531
Linda Sorensen: Yes, this works. Tyler, you have the calendar in front of you?

7
00:00:49.818 --> 00:00:59.973
Tyler Reed: I do. I pulled up the training invites before this call. So we've got the Signal AI session scheduled for the twenty-second at ten.

8
00:01:00.551 --> 00:01:10.174
Aisha Coleman: Perfect. And that's a two-hour block, correct? I want to make sure we have enough time for the QM scorecard walkthrough too.

9
00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.778
Tyler Reed: Actually, I think I only put an hour on the invite. Let me double-check.

10
00:01:16.573 --> 00:01:24.958
Aisha Coleman: No worries. If it's an hour, we can cover the basics and then add a follow-up for the scorecard piece. Either way works.

11
00:01:25.262 --> 00:01:32.444
Linda Sorensen: One hour might be tight. The compliance team will want to be on that call, and they always have questions.

12
00:01:33.043 --> 00:01:41.910
Aisha Coleman: Okay, so maybe we split it. Session one for the general overview and session two for the scorecard configuration. Would that be easier for your team?

13
00:01:42.298 --> 00:01:47.021
Linda Sorensen: I think so. Let's do two sessions. That way nobody feels rushed.

14
00:01:47.839 --> 00:01:59.875
Aisha Coleman: Great. Tyler, can you send updated invites for both? I'll hold the same times on my end. What about the week after, is there anything on the calendar I should know about?

15
00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:10.850
Tyler Reed: The week of the twenty-eighth is a bit full. We have a board meeting on the thirtieth. But the mornings are usually open.

16
00:02:12.092 --> 00:02:19.755
Aisha Coleman: Mornings work for me. Let's target Tuesday or Wednesday morning for session two. I'll send a couple of options.

17
00:02:20.594 --> 00:02:23.599
Tyler Reed: Sounds good. I'll look out for those.

18
00:02:24.202 --> 00:02:33.958
Aisha Coleman: Now, on the user side. You mentioned last time you had a few new hires starting in October. Are we still looking at three additional QM seats?

19
00:02:34.693 --> 00:02:41.514
Linda Sorensen: Yes, three new member experience specialists. They start on the fifth. Tyler, can we get them set up before then?

20
00:02:43.014 --> 00:02:53.381
Tyler Reed: I'll need their names and email addresses. Once I have those, I can add them to the Invoca platform and assign the QM role.

21
00:02:54.294 --> 00:03:07.394
Aisha Coleman: I can help with that. I'll send over a quick template for the user details. If you get it back to me by the first, I'll make sure the accounts are ready.

22
00:03:08.023 --> 00:03:11.156
Tyler Reed: Perfect. I'll get that to you by Friday.

23
00:03:11.593 --> 00:03:17.389
Aisha Coleman: Thank you. And Linda, any changes on the team structure I should be aware of?

24
00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:26.990
Linda Sorensen: No, same structure. Just the three new hires. We did promote one of our senior specialists to a team lead role, but that doesn't change their Invoca access.

25
00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:39.425
Aisha Coleman: Got it. I'll note that. Now, I also wanted to touch on seasonal volume. You mentioned the fall lending push. Is there anything we should plan for in terms of call tracking numbers?

26
00:03:40.268 --> 00:03:48.009
Tyler Reed: We've already added a few new tracking numbers for the auto loan campaign. That's been live for about two weeks.

27
00:03:49.435 --> 00:03:56.963
Aisha Coleman: Okay. And those are routing to the right queues? I just want to confirm before we get deeper into the season.

28
00:03:58.031 --> 00:04:01.961
Tyler Reed: Yes, they're routing correctly. I tested a few calls myself.

29
00:04:02.406 --> 00:04:10.633
Aisha Coleman: Great. If anything changes, just let me know. I know you have the Google Ads integration set up for offline conversions.

30
00:04:10.633 --> 00:04:12.592
Aisha Coleman: Is that still running smoothly?

31
00:04:14.055 --> 00:04:16.114
Tyler Reed: It's fine. No issues there.

32
00:04:17.606 --> 00:04:20.540
Aisha Coleman: Good. And Salesforce Financial Services Cloud, same?

33
00:04:21.548 --> 00:04:23.124
Tyler Reed: Yes, that's fine too.

34
00:04:23.559 --> 00:04:36.677
Aisha Coleman: Excellent. So next steps from my side: I'll send the user template and the updated training invites. Linda, do you want me to include the compliance team on the scorecard session?

35
00:04:36.909 --> 00:04:45.663
Linda Sorensen: Yes, please. I'll forward the invite to them once I have it. They'll want to review the scorecard before we finalize anything.

36
00:04:46.535 --> 00:04:52.481
Aisha Coleman: Understood. I'll mark it as required for them. Anything else on your end before we wrap up?

37
00:04:53.263 --> 00:04:55.706
Tyler Reed: I think that's it. Thanks, Aisha.

38
00:04:56.406 --> 00:04:58.774
Linda Sorensen: Thanks for your help. Talk soon.

39
00:04:59.761 --> 00:05:05.737
Aisha Coleman: Thank you both. I'll follow up with the emails today. Have a great rest of your week.
